# PORT03, second cflib client: TeraDesk. No gesture -- the run only has to show
# that DESKTOP.NAP, relinked against the new cflib.a, comes up. It is started
# through the project's own mechanism, the #Z autorun line in C:\NEWDESK.INF
# (method/newdesk-tera.inf), not by a scripted click.
#
# With #Z, TeraDesk is started INSTEAD of our desktop, so DESK_UP is never set
# and the injector (which t10_workaround.py gates on DESK_UP) never arms --
# measured in the first attempt of this run, whose log stops at
# "[shell] sh_ldapp: starting C:\APPS\TERADESK\DESKTOP.NAP" with no [h02] line.
# The screendump is therefore triggered on THAT kernel line plus a settle, not
# on an injector mark; this action list stays only so the injector is armed the
# same way as in the QED run.
100 parkbr
1000 arm
1200 mark A_DESK
8000 mark B_TERA
12000 pause
